<% seo title: "Pricing · Tastatur",
       description: "Two plans, priced on events stored rather than people tracked. Unlimited " \
                    "teammates on both, no overage charge, and self-hosting is free of both.",
       structured_data: :pricing %>

<div class="shell">
  <section class="rule-heavy pt-8 pb-12">
    <p class="label mb-5">Pricing</p>
    <h1 class="text-[clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem)] font-semibold leading-[1.06] tracking-[-0.035em] max-w-2xl">
      Two plans. Both of them<br>count events, not people.
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-ink-2 mt-6 max-w-xl leading-relaxed">
      Priced on the events we store for you, because that is the thing that costs us
      anything. Teammates are unlimited on both — an analytics tool nobody can afford
      to give access to is an analytics tool nobody reads.
    </p>
  </section>

  <%# --- The plans, side by side on one grid so the numbers line up. --------- -%>
  <section class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-px bg-rule">
    <% @plans.each do |plan| %>
      <div class="bg-surface p-8 flex flex-col">
        <p class="label <%= "text-signal" if plan.paid? %>"><%= plan.name %></p>

        <p class="mt-4 flex items-baseline gap-2">
          <span class="text-[40px] font-semibold tracking-[-0.03em] leading-none num">
            $<%= plan.price_display %>
          </span>
          <span class="text-sm text-muted"><%= plan.paid? ? "per month" : "forever" %></span>
        </p>

        <dl class="mt-8 space-y-0">
          <% [
               ["Events a month", number_with_delimiter(plan.monthly_event_limit)],
               ["Sites", plan.unlimited_sites? ? "Unlimited" : plan.site_limit.to_s],
               ["Teammates", "Unlimited"],
               ["Data retention", "Up to #{Account::MAX_RETENTION_DAYS / 30} months, your choice"],
               ["Shared dashboards", "Included"],
               ["Goals and funnels", "Included"]
             ].each do |term, value| %>
            <%# `sm:shrink-0`, not `shrink-0`: on a phone "Data retention" plus
                its value is wider than the row, and a value that cannot shrink
                can only overflow. Below `sm` it wraps instead. %>
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 border-t border-rule py-3">
              <dt class="text-sm text-ink-2"><%= term %></dt>
              <dd class="text-sm font-medium num sm:shrink-0 text-right"><%= value %></dd>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </dl>

        <div class="mt-8 pt-2">
          <% if user_signed_in? %>
            <%= link_to plan.paid? ? "Upgrade" : "Your current options", billing_path,
                        class: "btn #{'btn-primary' if plan.paid?}" %>
          <% elsif Tastatur.allow_signup? %>
            <%= link_to plan.paid? ? "Start on #{plan.name}" : "Start free", new_user_registration_path,
                        class: "btn #{'btn-primary' if plan.paid?}" %>
          <% else %>
            <%= link_to "Sign in", new_user_session_path, class: "btn" %>
          <% end %>
        </div>

        <p class="text-[12px] text-muted mt-4 leading-relaxed">
          <% if plan.paid? %>
            Cancel any time, from the same portal you pay in. No annual commitment and
            no per-seat pricing.
          <% else %>
            No card, no trial clock. Upgrade if and when you outgrow it.
          <% end %>
        </p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# --- What happens at the limit. Stated here rather than found out later. - -%>
  <section class="py-16 border-t border-rule grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <p class="label mb-5">What the limit actually does</p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.025em]">
        We stop recording.<br>We do not bill you<br>for going over.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-5 text-[15px] text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        <strong class="text-ink">There is no overage charge.</strong> Once an account passes
        its monthly allowance, further events are not recorded, and the allowance resets on
        the first of the month. You will never get an invoice larger than the price above.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong class="text-ink">You are told before it happens.</strong> The account's
        owner gets an email at 80% and again if the allowance runs out, and the figure is
        on the plan screen the whole time. A quota nobody warned you about is indistinguishable
        from a broken installation.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong class="text-ink">Bots do not count.</strong> Crawler traffic is dropped
        before it is stored, and so are events claiming a hostname that is not yours. Neither
        reaches your allowance, so none of it is spent on measurement you cannot read.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong class="text-ink">Downgrading never deletes anything.</strong> Cancel while
        you have twenty sites and all twenty keep collecting; you simply cannot add a
        twenty-first until you are back under the limit. Nor does the month you are in get
        cut short: an account that has already recorded more than the smaller plan covers
        still gets that plan's full allowance for the rest of that month. Your data is yours,
        and a billing event is not a reason to destroy it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <%# --- The third option, which is free in the other sense. ---------------- -%>
  <section class="py-16 border-t border-rule grid lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <p class="label mb-5">Or don't pay us at all</p>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.025em]">Self-host it.<br>No limits, no billing.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <p class="text-[15px] text-ink-2 leading-relaxed">
        Tastatur is AGPL-3.0 and the hosted service runs the same code you can. A
        self-hosted install has no plans, no event ceiling and no Stripe: it is one
        environment variable, and the upgrade interface disappears entirely. You bring
        PostgreSQL with TimescaleDB and a Redis, and you own every row.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-7">
        <%= link_to "Read the source", Tastatur.maintainer[:source], class: "btn", rel: "noopener" %>
        <%= link_to "What it collects", privacy_path, class: "btn btn-quiet" %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
